usage: lab-twin [-h]
                [--mode {sim,replay,live,build-twin,pretrain,train,evaluate,calibrate,hil-test}]
                [--config CONFIG] [--seed SEED] [--input INPUT]
                [--output OUTPUT] [--checkpoint CHECKPOINT]
                [--mae-checkpoint MAE_CHECKPOINT] [--device {cpu,cuda,auto}]
                [--headless] [--max-frames MAX_FRAMES] [--duration DURATION]
                [--epochs EPOCHS] [--record RECORD] [--twin TWIN] [--mobile]
                [--rebuild-twin] [--commissioning-mode {auto,mobile,stations}]
                [--websocket] [--threads THREADS]
                [--render-backend {auto,native,mesa}] [--mesa-dir MESA_DIR]
                [--real-time]

Unified, explicit CLI for the lab digital twin.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --mode {sim,replay,live,build-twin,pretrain,train,evaluate,calibrate,hil-test}
  --config CONFIG
  --seed SEED
  --input INPUT
  --output OUTPUT
  --checkpoint CHECKPOINT
  --mae-checkpoint MAE_CHECKPOINT
  --device {cpu,cuda,auto}
  --headless
  --max-frames MAX_FRAMES
  --duration DURATION   Wall-clock run duration, seconds
  --epochs EPOCHS
  --record RECORD
  --twin TWIN
  --mobile
  --rebuild-twin
  --commissioning-mode {auto,mobile,stations}
                        Explicitly declare independent at-rest station
                        captures when timestamps reset
  --websocket
  --threads THREADS
  --render-backend {auto,native,mesa}
  --mesa-dir MESA_DIR
  --real-time           Pace replay/simulation at acquisition time when
                        processing is faster
